== Cultural Significance == These shrines represent the fusion of Shinto and Buddhist practices unique to Kumano Pilgrimage culture. Many are associated with legends, poetry, and historical figures, such as [[:en:Izumi Shikibu|Izumi Shikibu]] and [[:en:Fujiwara no Teika|Fujiwara no Teika]].
== Access == * '''Nearest Station:''' [[:en:Shingū Station|Shingū Station]] (JR [[:en:Kisei Main Line|Kisei Main Line]]) * Bus services from [[:en:Kii-Tanabe Station|Kii-Tanabe Station]] via {{ill|Ryujin Bus|ja|龍神バス|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ryujin Bus|qq=|ja_comment=jawiki redirects to 龍神自動車|1=Ryūjin Bus|comment=changed title based on wikidata|WD=Q11679334}}
